# =============================================================================
# ALLOWLIST .gitignore
#
# Nothing in this repository is tracked unless it is named explicitly below.
# Data, results, caches, credentials, and scratch files are excluded by
# default and do not need their own rules.
#
# HOW TO ADD A FILE
#   1. If it lives in a folder, un-ignore the folder chain first (see the
#      FOLDERS block). Git will not look inside an ignored folder, so a rule
#      for a file inside one never fires.
#   2. Add one "!path/to/file" line to the FILES block.
#   3. Verify before committing:  git status --porcelain
#
# Add nothing below the FILES block. Later rules override earlier ones, so a
# pattern placed after the allowlist would silently re-ignore your files.
# =============================================================================


# --- 1. Ignore everything ----------------------------------------------------

*


# --- 2. FOLDERS: open the path to each tracked file --------------------------
# Each folder needs two lines: un-ignore the folder, then re-ignore its
# contents. Copy the pair for any new folder.

!Code/
Code/*

!Notebooks/
Notebooks/*

# Uncomment as needed:
!SQL/
SQL/*


# --- 3. FILES: the complete list of what gets committed ----------------------
# One line per file. This is the only place to add anything.

!.gitignore
!README.md
!LICENSE

!Code/HPT_Analysis_Pipeline.R
!Code/HPT_warm_start.R
!Code/HPT_diagnostic_for_family_levels.R


!Notebooks/HPT_Python_Pipeline.ipynb

# Examples, uncomment and edit:
!SQL/01_Phase1_Codebook.sql
!SQL/02_Phase2to4_Prices.sql
!SQL/03_Supplementary_Analyses.sql
# !HPT_Project.Rproj

# --- end of allowlist. Do not add patterns below this line. ---